    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "给 + person + verb: doing something for or to someone",
      "body": "To say who you call, put 给 and the person before the verb: 给妈妈打电话 means 'call Mom'. The same pattern works for doing things for someone, like cooking or buying. The person always comes right after 给, and the action comes after the person.",
      "examples": [
